Intel Graphics Compiler (IGC) is an LLVM-based compiler for OpenCL
and compute shaders targeting Intel graphics hardware, including
Intel Arc discrete GPUs. It is a required runtime dependency of
intel-compute-runtime (NEO), the OpenCL and Level Zero driver.

This build bundles its own copies of LLVM 16, SPIRV-Tools,
SPIRV-Headers, SPIRV-LLVM-Translator, vc-intrinsics, and
opencl-clang at the versions required by IGC. Do not attempt to
substitute system versions of these components.

Due to the bundled LLVM compilation, this build requires significant
resources: allow at least 10GB of free disk space and 8GB of RAM.
Build time may exceed one hour depending on hardware.

All source tarballs listed in intel-graphics-compiler.info must be
downloaded and placed in the SlackBuild directory before building.
